ence relations.\n    It computes even terms first, then resolves odd terms' forward dependencies.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The sequence needs values up to tri(n+1) to resolve forward dependencies for odd tri(n)\n    # So, the memoization table will store values from tri(0) to tri(n+1).\n    # The list size will be (n + 1) + 1 = n + 2.\n    memo = [0] * (n + 2)\n\n    # Base cases for tri(0) and tri(1)\n    memo[0] = 1  # Inferred from example: tri(3) = [1, 3, 2, 8]\n    memo[1] = 3  # Given by the problem statement\n\n    # First pass: Calculate all even terms up to tri(n+1).\n    # These terms do not have forward dependencies.\n    for k in range(2, n + 2):\n        if k % 2 == 0:  # k is even\n            memo[k] = 1 + k // 2  # Use integer division as implied by examples\n\n    # Second pass: Calculate all odd terms from tri(n+1) down to tri(2).\n    # This backward iteration ensures that tri(k+1) is already computed when needed for tri(k).\n    for k in range(n + 1, 1, -1):  # Iterate from n+1 down to 2 (exclusive of 1)\n        if k % 2 != 0:  # k is odd\n            # tri(k) = tri(k - 1) + tri(k - 2) + tri(k + 1)\n            memo[k] = memo[k - 1] + memo[k - 2] + memo[k + 1]\n\n    # Return the first n+1 numbers of the sequence (tri(0) to tri(n))\n    return memo[:n + 1]", "base_status": "fail", "plus_status": "fail", "base_fail_tests": [[4]], "plus_fail_tests": [[2]]}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/130", "solution": "def tri(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Tribonacci sequence as defined by recurrence relations and returns the first n+1 numbers.\n    Memoization is used to efficiently handle recursive calls and forward dependencies.\n    \"\"\"\n    _memo = {}\n\n    def _get_tribonacci_number(k):\n        \"\"\"Helper function to calculate a single Tribonacci number tri(k) using memoization.\"\"\"\n        if k in _memo:\n            return _memo[k]\n\n        if k == 1:\n            value = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # k is even (includes k=0)\n            value = 1 